      "text": "Car explosion injures person in Syria’s Manbij\n\nThe city of Manbij, northern Syria – North Press/Archive\n\nMANBIJ, Syria (North Press) – A car explosion in the village of Hassan Agha, south of Manbij in northern Syria, injured a person on Sunday.\n\nAn eyewitness told North Press that the person was slightly injured while in a mosque in the village.\n\nThe injured person was identified as Ahmed al-Jassim, 44, from Hassan Agha, according to the source.\n\nManbij Military Council posted on Facebook that a Turkish drone targeted a civilian car, causing the injury to al-Jassim.\n\nThis incident comes after three people were killed in Manbij on July 9 in a similar car targeting.\n\nAnadolu Agency reported on Saturday that Turkish intelligence was responsible for the previous targeting.\n\nReporting by Fadi al-Hussein"
    }
